-- title:
--   Completed stalk at a supersingular point: regular, with Drinfeld basis
-- statement:
--   Fix primes $q\ge 5$ and $\ell\ge 3$ with $\ell\neq q$, and $M'\neq 0$ divisible by neither $q$ nor $\ell$; let $L$ be a field of characteristic $0$ that is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of type $\{q\ell\}$, containing a primitive $q$-th root of unity $\zeta$ and a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity $\xi$. Let $K$ be the intermediate field of $L \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ generated over $L$ by the coefficientwise image of the function field [`ModularCurve.xHFunctionField ((q*ℓ)^2*M')`](def/ModularCurve_XH.html#L79) of level $H=\ker\bigl((\mathbb{Z}/(q\ell)^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb{Z}/q\ell)^\times\bigr)$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation ring with fraction field $L$, with $q$ in its maximal ideal, with $\zeta$ in the image of $A$, acting on $K$ compatibly with $L$, and with uniformiser $\varpi$; let $j\in K$ be nonzero with Laurent expansion the coefficient-embedded $q$-expansion [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157). Let $z$ be a point of the two-chart integral model $\mathfrak{X}=$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236) (the pushout of the spectra of the integral closure of $A[j]$ in $K$ and of the chart at infinity) such that the germ at $z$ of the global section induced by $\varpi$ via $\mathfrak{X}\to\operatorname{Spec} A$ lies in the maximal ideal of the stalk, let $y$ be a point of $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the finite chart algebra $C=$ `chartAlgFin A K j` mapping to $z$, and assume $y$ is supersingular in the sense that for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi\colon C\to\Omega$ with kernel the prime of $y$, the value $\varphi(j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), i.e. every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\Omega$ with that $j$-invariant has no nonzero point killed by $q$. Then there exist: a noetherian local ring $R_0$, complete for its maximal-ideal-adic topology, with finite residue field of characteristic $q$; a complete discrete valuation ring $W_1$ with a ring homomorphism $\sigma\colon A\to W_1$ whose maximal ideal is generated by $\sigma\varpi$ and a unit $\varepsilon_1$ with $(\sigma\varpi)^{q-1}=\varepsilon_1 q$; a local homomorphism $\iota_1\colon W_1\to R_0$; a ring isomorphism $\beta$ from the maximal-ideal-adic completion of the stalk of $\mathfrak{X}$ at $z$ onto $R_0$; a commutative formal group $F$ over $R_0$ and $x_0,x_1\in R_0$ forming a Drinfeld basis of level $q$ for $F$ relative to the maximal ideal, with $\mathfrak{m}_{R_0}=(x_0,x_1)$; elements $T,w\in R_0$ with $w$ a unit and $\mathrm{coeff}_q(F.\mathrm{nthSeries}\,q)-wT\in qR_0$, where `nthSeries q` is the $q$-fold iterate $[q]_F$; witnesses that the Laurent series [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L (q*ℓ)`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18) lies in $K$ and that the resulting element lies in $C$; and $a_0\in W_1$, $k\ge 1$, a unit $w'\in R_0$, such that $R_0$ is a regular local ring of Krull dimension $2$, $\beta$ carries the image in the completion of the germ at $z$ of the section induced by any $a\in A$ to $\iota_1(\sigma a)$, and $\beta$ of the image in the completion of the germ at $z$ (through the finite chart) of that element of $C$ satisfies $\beta(\cdot)-\iota_1 a_0 = w'T^k$.
--
--   This is the ring-theoretic form of the local description of the integral model of the modular curve at a supersingular point in characteristic $q$: the completed stalk is a two-dimensional complete regular local ring carrying a formal group with a Drinfeld basis of level $q$ generating the maximal ideal, the Hasse parameter $T$ appears as the $Z^q$-coefficient of $[q]_F$ modulo $q$, and the germ of the level-$q\ell$ reparametrised $j$-expansion is a unit times a power of $T$ after subtracting a constant. It is the input consumed by the subsequent statement that produces a power-series chart at such a point, where the residue field and Hasse data are read off.
